From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 13:38:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] pipeline: simple: Skip capture sizes the video node does
 not support

tryPipeline() adds a configuration for every pixel format the video
node offers for the propagated media bus code, ignoring the frame sizes
it reports. A capture device with a width step then gets configured for
a size it cannot produce, and configure() fails late with "Unable to
configure capture". Skip the formats whose size ranges do not contain
the capture size.

On MediaTek's CAMSV, which takes widths in steps of 8, this stops the
IMX111's 820x614 mode from being picked for the viewfinder.

Tested on a Zinwa Q25 (MT6789, IMX111).
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index 79efc8e9..62ac67e8 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -735,6 +735,18 @@ void SimpleCameraData::tryPipeline(unsigned int code, const Size &size)
 			continue;
 		}
 
+		const std::vector<SizeRange> &sizes = videoFormat.second;
+		if (!sizes.empty() &&
+		    std::none_of(sizes.begin(), sizes.end(),
+				 [&](const SizeRange &range) {
+					 return range.contains(format.size);
+				 })) {
+			LOG(SimplePipeline, Debug)
+				<< "Capture size " << format.size
+				<< " not supported in " << videoFormat.first;
+			continue;
+		}
+
 		Configuration config;
 		config.code = code;
 		config.sensorSize = size;
